+# Cedar Grove Volunteer Celebration
+
+## Confirmed event
+
+- Host: Cedar Grove Arts Collective
+- Event: Cedar Grove Volunteer Celebration
+- Date: Sunday, October 18, 2026
+- Time: 2:00–5:00 p.m.
+- Venue: Maple Room, Lumen House
+- Address: 1842 West Armitage Avenue, Chicago, Illinois 60622
+- Attendance: 48 people
+- RSVP deadline: October 9, 2026
+
+## Run of show
+
+| Start | End | Activity | Lead | Operational note |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| 2:00 p.m. | 2:20 p.m. | Guest arrival and check-in | Welcome team | Place name badges at the west doors |
+| 2:20 p.m. | 2:30 p.m. | Welcome | Program director | Use the house microphone |
+| 2:30 p.m. | 3:15 p.m. | Buffet service | Catering captain | Release tables one at a time |
+| 3:15 p.m. | 3:50 p.m. | Volunteer stories | Story hosts | Introduce three confirmed speakers |
+| 3:50 p.m. | 4:15 p.m. | Recognition | Board chair | Present awards in surname order |
+| 4:15 p.m. | 4:50 p.m. | Community mingle | All staff | Keep the east alcove available for quiet seating |
+| 4:50 p.m. | 5:00 p.m. | Closing and departure | Program director | Direct departing guests to the west doors |
+
+## Setup and accessibility
+
+Set six round tables with eight places each, for 48 places total. At two center-aisle tables, configure one of the eight places as a chair-free wheelchair position, leaving seven chairs and one wheelchair position at each of those tables. Mark the table nearest the east alcove as quiet seating. Keep a clear center aisle from the staffed elevator to the quiet seating and the front of the room. The step-free west doors are the guest entrance. Put out 48 large-print programs, one at every place, and position wayfinding signs at the west doors and elevator. Before guests arrive, test the house microphone and projection screen.
+
+## Catering
+
+| Item | Quantity | Unit cost | Line total |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|
+| Garden Table buffet | 48 | $26.00 | $1248.00 |
+| Citrus Sparkler station | 48 | $4.00 | $192.00 |
+| Total | — | — | $1440.00 |
+
+The selected buffet provides a vegetarian base menu with vegan and gluten-free portions included when the final quantity is supplied. The nonalcoholic beverage station includes citrus and plain sparkling water, cups, and ice.
+
+## Attendee message
+
+**Subject:** Cedar Grove Volunteer Celebration — Sunday, October 18
+
+**Body:** Please join Cedar Grove Arts Collective for the Cedar Grove Volunteer Celebration on Sunday, October 18, 2026, from 2:00–5:00 p.m. in the Maple Room at Lumen House, 1842 West Armitage Avenue, Chicago, Illinois 60622. Please arrive through the step-free west doors, where guest check-in will be located. Route 8 stops across from Lumen House at the west-door stop. RSVP by October 9, 2026. To request access accommodations, note them in the RSVP form; the venue also has a staffed elevator and quiet seating near the east alcove. We look forward to celebrating with you.
+
+## Coordinator checklist
+
+- Begin room setup when event-team access opens at 1:00 p.m.
+- Place check-in, name badges, and wayfinding signs at the west doors and elevator.
+- Test the house microphone and projection screen before doors open.
+- Set out 48 large-print programs and mark the east-alcove quiet seating.
+- Finish teardown and leave the Maple Room completely clear by 5:45 p.m.
